From 0e1cee1ab2a4862c60e3756b3f8810e1aa53e6cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:24:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] httpd: every client list fills on a box that is not routing;
 the diag collector runs detached from the request

GT-BE19000 tester, Access Point mode (2026-10-02): the Network page's Main
Network card showed 0 devices and its Clients tab "No device connected" while
the AiMesh node card (fixed in v3.3.1) counted them. Owner: fix it for every
menu, at the source.

- ej_get_clientlist(): on a non-routing box (rdev_nonrouting(): sw_mode not
  router or hotspot) the hook merges Reaper's device store. networkmap sets
  isOnline from DHCP leases and conntrack, which a bridging box does not have,
  so every stock surface on that hook - the Network page's cards and Clients
  tab, Parental Controls, the QoS pickers, the topology node card - read empty
  there. A row networkmap produced is kept and marked present (ip, band,
  network and node filled where it left them blank); a device it does not know
  is added in its own shape with from = "reaper_dev". Nodes, backhaul stations
  and affiliated MLO links are not devices and are left out, as the Devices
  page leaves them.
- rdev_collect(): the scan that was the body of reaper_dev.cgi action=status
  (steps 1-7 unchanged) is now one collector for both callers, cached as a
  snapshot for the hook - it is polled every 10 s by several pages and the scan
  popen()s wl per VIF and brctl per bridge on a single-flight httpd. The status
  action still takes a fresh pass. New at the end: every present device gets a
  network - cfg_mnt's own answer, else the VIF map (vif_used), else the bridge
  the cable was learned on (the FDB scan now walks br0 and every enabled SDN's
  own bridge, where a guest or IoT VLAN's wired clients are learned), else the
  main fronthaul row.
- do_reaper_diag_cgi (perf audit P2): the collector ran INLINE - popen()
  drained to EOF inside the single-threaded httpd, so every diagnostic run
  froze the whole GUI and the login page for the length of the collection. It
  is now a detached grandchild (rdiag_worker, the rwifi sampler's shape) that
  writes OK <path> or ERR to /tmp/.reaper_diag_state; the page asks
  action=start, polls action=status every 2 s (cap 5 min) and fetches
  action=get. start reclaims a lock older than 180 s; status says RUNNING only
  while the lock is under 300 s old. The CSRF gate, the lock and the
  /tmp/reaper_diag_ path contract are unchanged; no dictionary change.
- get_client_detail_info (perf audit P30): nmp_wl_offline_check is written
  only when it is not already "1" - it was one nvram write per clientlist GET
  on a 3-10 s poller.

Tests: build-scripts/tests/test_apmode_surfaces.py section 6 compiles
rdev_sdn_of_bridge, rdev_sdn_of_vif_in and rdev_sta_sdn from source (13
checks) and asserts the hook's merge; verify_markers "diag collector started
detached" plus the page's start and status literals.

